sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: To find the greatest common measure of three given numbers not relatively prime.
----
proof:

Let {A}, {B}, and {C} be the three given numbers not relatively prime.

It is required to find the greatest common measure of {A}, {B}, and {C}.

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="210" height="250" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="VII.3 diagram" src="propVII3.gif"/></noscript>
<script type="text/javascript">
    // Numbers as vertical segments: A = 6, B = 4, C = 3, D = 2, E = F = 1
    // in units of E, all built by cutoffs from E's length. Nothing is added
    // to the figure; the walk brings D, E and F on with the sentences that
    // introduce them and otherwise lights the numbers each step names.
    //
    // Joyce's figure is drawn for the second case (D does not measure C).
    // In the first case "some number E, greater than D" is a hypothetical
    // number, not the figure's E (the greatest common measure of D and C,
    // and less than D), so that E is left untokenized in the case-one
    // captions and prose, and the figure's E stays off until slide 25.
    // F in the second case is the figure's F, drawn by Joyce equal to E.
    var GIVEN = ["A","B","C"];
    var WITHD = GIVEN.concat(["D","D1"]);
    var WITHE = WITHD.concat(["E","E1","E2"]);
    var WITHF = WITHE.concat(["F","F1"]);
