              highlighted: ["D","C"] },
            { text: "I say first that {C} and {D} are not relatively prime.",
              visible: WITHD,
              highlighted: ["C","D"] },
            { text: "Since {A}, {B}, and {C} are not relatively prime, therefore some number measures them.",
              visible: WITHD,
              highlighted: ["A","B","C"] },
            { text: "Now that which measures {A}, {B}, and {C} also measures {A} and {B},",
              visible: WITHD,
              highlighted: ["A","B"] },
            { text: "and therefore measures {D}, the greatest common measure of {A} and {B}.",
              visible: WITHD,
              highlighted: ["D"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "a common measure measures the GCM", ref: "VII.2,Cor." }] },
            { text: "But it measures {C} also, therefore some number measures the numbers {D} and {C}.",
              visible: WITHD,
              highlighted: ["D","C"] },
            { text: "Therefore {D} and {C} are not relatively prime.",
              visible: WITHD,
              highlighted: ["D","C"] },
            { text: "Take their greatest common measure {E}.",
              visible: WITHE,
              highlighted: ["D","C","E"],
              transition: { animations: [
